<% content_for :title, "Getting Started" %>
<% content_for :description, "Start using recuerd0 with your AI tools: connect through the portable agent skill, Claude Code plugin, or MCP, then grow the three-memory starter shape." %>
<% content_for :canonical_url, "https://recuerd0.ai/start" %>

<div data-controller="marketing-sidebar">
  <%= render "pages/doc_header", section: "Getting Started" %>

  <aside class="doc-sidebar" data-marketing-sidebar-target="sidebar">
    <div class="sidebar-group">
      <div class="sidebar-heading">Getting Started</div>
      <a href="#path" class="sidebar-link active" data-section="path" data-action="click->marketing-sidebar#closeSidebar">The path</a>
      <a href="#doors" class="sidebar-link" data-section="doors" data-action="click->marketing-sidebar#closeSidebar">Choose a door</a>
      <a href="#shape" class="sidebar-link" data-section="shape" data-action="click->marketing-sidebar#closeSidebar">Why this shape</a>
    </div>
  </aside>

  <main class="doc-main">
    <div class="doc-content">
      <div class="page-header">
        <h1>Getting Started</h1>
        <p>Start with the three memories already waiting for you, connect the AI tools you use, and let the structure grow only when your work asks for it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="api-section" id="path">
        <div class="resource-header">
          <h2>The path</h2>
          <p>A new account opens with a <strong>Start Here</strong> workspace and three memories in a deliberate reading order.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="endpoint-head">
          <h3>1. Read the map</h3>
          <p><code>_MAP</code> is the front door. Read it first in every session and add one plain-language line whenever you add a memory.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="endpoint-head">
          <h3>2. Carry the work forward</h3>
          <p><code>Continuation Brief</code> is the second read. Rewrite it at the end of a working session with the current state, open threads, and the next thing to do.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="endpoint-head">
          <h3>3. Keep decisions reachable</h3>
          <p><code>_INDEX — Decisions</code> holds one line per locked decision. Give the full decision its own memory and point to it from the index.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="section-divider"></div>

      <div class="api-section" id="doors">
        <div class="resource-header">
          <h2>Choose a door</h2>
          <p>Connect through the portable agent skill, the native Claude Code plugin, or MCP. They all reach the same memories.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="endpoint-head">
          <h3>Portable agent skill</h3>
          <p>Install the <%= link_to "recuerd0 CLI", cli_path %>, add an account with a personal access token, then install the skill for the agents detected on your machine.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-block" data-controller="clipboard">
          <div class="code-head"><span class="code-label">install the CLI</span><%= render "pages/code_copy" %></div>
          <div class="code-body"><code data-clipboard-target="source">curl -fsSL https://github.com/maquina-app/recuerd0-cli/releases/latest/download/install.sh | sh</code></div>
        </div>
        <div class="code-block" data-controller="clipboard">
          <div class="code-head"><span class="code-label">connect your account</span><%= render "pages/code_copy" %></div>
          <div class="code-body"><code data-clipboard-target="source">recuerd0 account add personal --api-url https://recuerd0.ai --token YOUR_TOKEN</code></div>
        </div>
        <div class="code-block" data-controller="clipboard">
          <div class="code-head"><span class="code-label">install the skill</span><%= render "pages/code_copy" %></div>
          <div class="code-body"><code data-clipboard-target="source">recuerd0 skills install</code></div>
        </div>

        <div class="endpoint-head">
          <h3>Claude Code plugin</h3>
          <p>Claude Code can install the same memory workflow directly from the maquina marketplace.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-block" data-controller="clipboard">
          <div class="code-head"><span class="code-label">Claude Code</span><%= render "pages/code_copy" %></div>
          <div class="code-body"><code data-clipboard-target="source">/plugin marketplace add maquina-app/rails-claude-code
/plugin install recuerd0@maquina</code></div>
        </div>

        <div class="endpoint-head">
          <h3>MCP</h3>
          <p>For Claude Desktop, Claude.ai, and other MCP clients, use the <%= link_to "remote MCP server", mcp_path %>. Authorization happens in the browser, so there is no personal token to paste into the client.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="section-divider"></div>

      <div class="api-section" id="shape">
        <div class="resource-header">
          <h2>Why this shape</h2>
          <p>Every session starts cold. The map orients it, the brief carries live state, and the index keeps durable decisions within two hops.</p>
        </div>

        <p class="doc-note">
          Keep the map flat until it gets crowded. Hubs are not seeded — you grow into them when a real cluster appears. Nothing about the starter workspace is enforced: rename it, trim it, or replace it with a shape that works better for you.
        </p>

        <p class="doc-note">
          Read the full reasoning in the
          <%= link_to "workspace blueprint", "https://github.com/maquina-app/recuerd0/blob/main/docs/blueprint.md", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%= render "pages/doc_footer" %>
  </main>
</div>
